# The raids half of the decoy mast (docs/VISION.md §9.3), on the real keys. A
# holding loud enough to be worth reading, a pole walked out past the last roof
# and put up there, a machine that stands at the pole and files THAT instead of
# the place, and a party that comes for the pole because that is what it was
# told about.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/decoy.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --holding=hut,hearth,radio_mast --attention=0.72 \
#     --give=timber:6,scrap:6,rag:6
#
# --holding stands the loud place up; building one is the settlements tour's
# proof and this one starts where a player reaches for an answer. --attention
# stages a holding already at the raid line, which is what living somewhere loud
# for days earns — and it is not a shortcut past the rule, because nothing is
# ever sent for a place nothing has read and it is the clerk in frame 04 that
# reads this one.
zoom 10
coast calm
wait 0.6
shot 01-a-holding-worth-reading with holding, piece:radio_mast, land:coast
# Out past the last roof, because in the yard a decoy is the yard. The holding
# key closes the page whether the slate took the piece or refused it, so a try
# that was not far enough out walks on with its hands free.
try 5
  walk 1,0 2.2
  tap holding
  await app:holding 4
  choose build_decoy_mast
  tap use
  wait 0.5
  tap holding
  await lure 3
end
walk -1,0 0.6
wait 1.0
shot 02-a-pole-out-past-the-yard with lure, piece:decoy_mast
# And the whole of what it is: twelve tiles of open ground between the rag and
# the last roof (Settlement.LURE_APART), which is the only reason a machine can
# stand at one and not be standing in the yard. Seen from halfway along it, the
# roofs at one end and the pole at the other.
walk -1,0 1.2
zoom 17
wait 0.8
shot 03-twelve-tiles-of-open-ground with lure, holding
zoom 10
walk 1,0 1.4
wait 0.6
# A clerk crosses the ground and reads the pole rather than the place. From this
# moment the record is a thing in the world, and it is a thing AT THE POLE: this
# is the ground it has to be caught on now, and the fence is the wrong ground.
spawn clerk
await lured 14
wait 0.4
shot 04-a-clerk-reads-the-decoy with mob:clerk, lure
# Let it go. What gets home is an account of a pole in a field — a quarter of
# what an account of the place is worth (Attention.LURED) — and the world says
# so on the glass.
await filed 30
wait 0.2
shot 05-what-the-plan-has-of-the-place with lure, holding
# The warning window runs out and a party comes out of the land. The harvester
# was sent for the loudest thing the plan has ever heard of this place, and that
# is the pole: it walks past the yard to a mast standing in a field.
hour 13.2
wait 1.6
await raid 30
await party 30
wait 0.8
shot 06-a-party-on-the-ground with mob, holding
await raid_damage 90
wait 0.3
shot 07-taking-the-decoy-apart with mob, lure
